# DURABLE REPRO — a FIXED-SIZE ARRAY in a function SIGNATURE (parameter or
# return type) is check-clean, BUILDS, and then prints GARBAGE.
#
# ⚠ The size here is a LITERAL. This is NOT the `meta`-constant array-size
# defect that R44 Track E fixed in `semantic/meta.rs substitute_type` — that
# one was a `gg check` REJECTION (`expected int[0], found int[3]`) and is now
# a live regression fixture (`tests/fixtures/known_gaps/meta_const_array_size_*.gg`).
# This one survives with `int[3]` spelled out, so it is a strictly separate,
# older defect in how a fixed-size array crosses a call boundary.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured 2026-08-23 at HEAD 4a16e4c5 + Track E, C backend):
#     gg check → OK: no semantic errors
#     gg run   → rc 0, prints two garbage integers, e.g.
#                  54606144574115712
#                  562947785007776
#                (values vary run to run — uninitialised stack)
#
# AXIS SAMPLED: the two SIGNATURE cells, parameter and return type. Both are
# in this one file because they share the symptom and (very likely) the
# mechanism: a fixed-size array has no by-value ABI, so the callee reads a
# slot that was never filled. The LOCAL-VARIABLE cell WORKS and is pinned
# live by `meta_const_array_size_local.gg` (prints 60), which is what makes
# this a signature-position defect rather than an arrays-are-broken defect.
# The STRUCT-FIELD cell is a different symptom (a C-compile failure) and has
# its own repro: `known_gaps/fixed_array_struct_field_cc_fail.gg`.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below):
#     60
#     60
int total(int[3] xs):
    return xs[0] + xs[1] + xs[2]

int[3] make():
    return [10, 20, 30]

int main():
    int[3] a = [10, 20, 30]
    print(total(a))
    int[3] b = make()
    print(b[0] + b[1] + b[2])
    return 0
